// supabase/functions/_shared/fonts.ts
//
// Subset typefaces, base64-embedded, for the PDF renderers (certificate.ts,
// factsheet.ts, and everything the sales library adds later).
//
// REGENERATED. The previous subset was cut for certificate.ts only, and the
// certificate deliberately never prints a score -- so it had no percent sign.
// The moment factsheet.ts drew "12.5%" and "80%", pdf-lib fell back to the
// missing-glyph box: a hollow rectangle in the domain weights and a black slug
// after the pass mark. It also broke the text layer, so copy-paste and search
// silently dropped the character too.
//
// A missing glyph fails LOUDLY on the page and SILENTLY in the text layer.
// That is why this subset is generous rather than minimal.
//
// COVERAGE
//   Basic Latin                U+0020-007E
//   Latin-1 Supplement         U+00A0-00FF   (a e i o u accents, n-tilde,
//                                             c-cedilla, a-tilde, o-tilde --
//                                             all of es-419 and pt-BR)
//   Latin Extended-A           U+0100-017F   Polish, Czech, Turkish, Baltic
//   General punctuation        dashes, quotes, bullet, ellipsis, per-mille
//   Symbols                    % S-section degree plus-minus euro tm arrows
//                              check cross <= >= != approx infinity
//
// LATIN EXTENDED-A IS NOT OPTIONAL. Certificates carry holder names. A
// tofu box in a candidate's own name is the worst possible defect on a
// credential, and it costs ~15 kB to prevent.
//
// SOURCES (both open licence, redistribution permitted)
//   Inter 4.1              -- SIL Open Font License 1.1, rsms/inter
//   JetBrains Mono 2.304   -- SIL Open Font License 1.1, JetBrains/JetBrainsMono
//
// REGENERATING
//   pyftsubset <src>.ttf --unicodes=<see scripts/build-fonts.md> \
//     --layout-features='kern' --no-hinting --desubroutinize \
//     --output-file=sub-<name>.ttf
//   then base64 each file into the constants below.
//
// AFTER REGENERATING, RE-RENDER A CERTIFICATE AND COMPARE IT.
// Font metrics differ between releases. certificate.ts positions text with
// hand-tuned coordinates, so a metric shift moves the holder name relative to
// the rule beneath it. A green build proves nothing here -- only looking does.

